# `def main()` is the first thing a Python program defines. On wasm32 the
# routine took the plain export name `main`, and the module entry wrapper then
# failed with `duplicate export "main"`; every other target built it. Module
# export names are now reserved and the routine is suffixed.
# bug-a-a-nilpy-function-named-main-is-refused-on-wasm32-only
def main():
    print("hello from main")
    return 3

def _start():
    return 4

print(main() + _start())
